feat 1.0

# ADR-0027: a negation takes one matcher, never another negation. `not not M` is `M`, so it is refused as MALFORMED_SYNTAX with a hint to write `M`.

spec SPEC-BAD-017 "Double negation"
context Bad
aggregate Thing
type command
status draft

construct:
  handler at src/do-thing.ts
  touches src/**

enforce:
  do the thing

contract:
  input ThingInput
  response ThingResult
  record ThingRow

scenario "does the thing":
  when: DoThing { value: 1 }
  predict success:
    response OK ThingResult
    eventStore has [ Wrote with ThingRow { ref: not not "x" } ]
